description:
CRITICAL CODE SMELL: Data Loss in Merge Function - Logic Bug

Location: src/intent/config.gleam, merge_with_flags function (line 65)

Root Cause:
  - timeout_ms field always uses override value without checking if it's default
  - Does not respect base config value when override is default value (30_000)
  - Other fields properly check for empty strings/false, but timeout_ms lacks this logic
  - Inconsistent merge behavior across fields

Before:
```gleam
pub fn merge_with_flags(base: Config, overrides: Config) -> Config {
  Config(
    target_url: case string.is_empty(overrides.target_url) {
      True -> base.target_url
      False -> overrides.target_url
    },
    allow_localhost: overrides.allow_localhost || base.allow_localhost,
    profile: case string.is_empty(overrides.profile) {
      True -> base.profile
      False -> overrides.profile
    },
    output_file: case string.is_empty(overrides.output_file) {
      True -> base.output_file
      False -> overrides.output_file
    },
    timeout_ms: overrides.timeout_ms,  // SMELL: Always uses override, loses base value!
  )
}
```

After:
```gleam
pub fn merge_with_flags(base: Config, overrides: Config) -> Config {
  Config(
    target_url: case string.is_empty(overrides.target_url) {
      True -> base.target_url
      False -> overrides.target_url
    },
    allow_localhost: overrides.allow_localhost || base.allow_localhost,
    profile: case string.is_empty(overrides.profile) {
      True -> base.profile
      False -> overrides.profile
    },
    output_file: case string.is_empty(overrides.output_file) {
      True -> base.output_file
      False -> overrides.output_file
    },
    timeout_ms: case overrides.timeout_ms == 30_000 {
      True -> base.timeout_ms  // If override is default, use base value
      False -> overrides.timeout_ms  // If explicitly set, use override
    },
  )
}
```

Impact: Configuration values silently lost during merge when override is default, violates merge semantics and data integrity principles

CODE SMELL: Duplicate Code - DRY Violation

Location: src/intent/formatter_utils.gleam, indent functions (lines 99-126)

Root Cause:
  - indent_0 through indent_4 duplicate indent_n logic
  - Copy-paste functions with hardcoded strings ("  ", "    ", etc.)
  - Single source of truth violated - indent_n exists but not used
  - Maintenance burden: change in spacing requires updating 5 places

Before:
```gleam
pub fn indent_0() -> String { "" }
pub fn indent_1() -> String { "  " }
pub fn indent_2() -> String { "    " }
pub fn indent_3() -> String { "      " }
pub fn indent_4() -> String { "        " }
pub fn indent_n(level: Int) -> String { string.repeat("  ", level) }
```

After - Option A (Minimal):
```gleam
pub fn indent(level: Int) -> String {
  indent_n(level)  // Single source of truth
}

pub fn indent_n(level: Int) -> String {
  string.repeat("  ", level)
}

// Remove: indent_0, indent_1, indent_2, indent_3, indent_4
```

After - Option B (Backward Compatible):
```gleam
pub fn indent_0() -> String { indent_n(0) }
pub fn indent_1() -> String { indent_n(1) }
pub fn indent_2() -> String { indent_n(2) }
pub fn indent_3() -> String { indent_n(3) }
pub fn indent_4() -> String { indent_n(4) }
pub fn indent_n(level: Int) -> String { string.repeat("  ", level) }
```

Recommendation: Use Option A (Minimal) - refactor callers to use indent_n directly

Impact: Code duplication makes maintenance harder, violates DRY principle, increases bug surface area
